note path-add, the command that does the real work. convert.rs has already read the trailing numbers: none or one is a whole symbol, two or three is a line range, and the last number is the parent when it is there. Default parent is the last step, so consecutive adds build a chain and an explicit index starts a branch; -1 is the root, and a parent past the last step is Failure::NoPlaceUnder. After the add it prints the step's index and parent, and the notes below.

